{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778980431192,"sessionID":"ses_1cc82e6b8ffeZCRAO8D6mymYrV","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"task","callID":"call_xqfLEXWAzsC0qVfHuQdg7zXc","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"parse porphyria spreadsheet","prompt":"You are analyzing a downloaded Excel workbook already extracted to XML files in /tmp/opencode: porphyria-sheet1.xml and porphyria-sharedStrings.xml. Reconstruct the meaningful contents of the worksheet 'Work here'. Focus on producing a concise structured summary of the requested MONDO changes for issue #9703: per row/term, extract identifiers, current and proposed names/definitions/parents/inheritance/gene-disease classification changes, notes, and any unresolved questions. Do not modify files. You may use read/grep/bash as needed. Return a compact but detailed table-like summary I can act on, and explicitly call out which rows appear actionable versus ambiguous.","subagent_type":"general","task_id":"","command":"analyze extracted porphyria workbook xml"},"output":"task_id: ses_1cc81ea29ffe1gjhh0yCubHcML (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\nBelow is a reconstruction of the meaningful content from worksheet `Work here` for MONDO issue `#9703`, based on `porphyria-sheet1.xml` plus `porphyria-sharedStrings.xml`.\n\n**Interpretation notes**\n- Rows `6, 10-13, 16, 18, 20` are continuation/detail rows for the gene block immediately above them.\n- `MONDO_...` values in the sheet appear to be MONDO IDs written with `_` instead of `:`.\n- I only report changes explicitly supported by the worksheet text. Where a parent/classification is implied rather than directly stated, I label it as such.\n\n**Structured Summary**\n\n| Sheet row(s) | Gene / focus | Current MONDO term(s) / disease labels in sheet | Requested MONDO change | Proposed revised name / new term | Proposed definition / disease model | Inheritance change | Parent / child / classification changes | Notes | Actionability |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `5-6` | `ALAS2` | `MONDO:0010420`; disease label `Protoporphyria, erythropoietic, X-linked`; extra linked OMIM label `Anemia, sideroblastic, 1` | `TERM Update (update definition + relabel)` | `ALAS2-related erythropoietic protoporphyria` | X-linked erythropoietic protoporphyria due to `gain-of-function` variants in terminal regulatory exon of `ALAS2`; clinically similar to FECH-related EPP | stays `XL`; sheet also lists `XLR` for sideroblastic anemia 1, supporting split | Explicitly says `Split from sideroblastic anemia 1`; rationale: `gene centric + primary site of heme synthesis affected is erythropoietic` | Strong signal that current ALAS2 term should be reframed away from sideroblastic anemia linkage and into porphyria naming | **Actionable** |\n| `7` | `ALAD` | `MONDO_0013000`; disease label `Porphyria, acute hepatic` | `TERM Update (update definition + relabel)` | `ALAD-related hepatic porphyria` | Hepatic porphyria due to `biallelic ALAD` variants; very rare; neurovisceral attacks without cutaneous manifestations | unchanged `AR` | Implied gene-centric hepatic porphyria classification; no child terms requested | Clean rename/definition update request | **Actionable** |\n| `9-13` | `HMBS` | No parent MONDO ID given for proposed parent. Existing terms listed: `MONDO_0958224 Encephalopathy, porphyria-related`; `MONDO_0958226 Leukoencephalopathy, porphyria-related`; `MONDO:0008294 Porphyria, acute intermittent`; plus `Porphyria, acute intermittent, nonerythroid variant` with `NOT AVAILABLE` MONDO ID | `NEW MONDO PARENT TERM TO (...) HMBS-related hepatic porphyria`; also `NEW Child Term: ACUTE INTERMITTENT PORPHYRIA NONERYTHROID VARIANT` | New parent: `HMBS-related hepatic porphyria`; new child term: `acute intermittent porphyria nonerythroid variant` | Parent term definition describes a semidominant HMBS disease spectrum: monoallelic adult acute attacks; biallelic severe childhood neurologic disease including developmental abnormalities, ataxia, dysarthria, leukoencephalopathy, cataracts, optic nerve hypoplasia. New child term definition: exon 1 / exon1-3 splicing-related subtype sparing erythrocyte isozyme | revised to `Semidominant` from mixed current `AR` and `AD` child rows | Explicit lumping request. Existing disease entities should become child terms of new parent. Additional request lists child names: acute intermittent porphyria, acute intermittent porphyria nonerythroid variant, porphyria-related leukoencephalopathy, porphyria-related encephalopathy | This is the most complex change set. Requires creation of a new parent term and at least one new child term, plus reparenting/reclassification of multiple existing terms | **Actionable, but multi-step** |\n| `14` | `UROS` | `MONDO_0009902`; disease label `Porphyria, congenital erythropoietic` | `TERM Update (update definition + relabel)` | `UROS-related erythropoietic porphyria` | AR erythropoietic porphyria due to `biallelic UROS` variants; severity stratified by residual enzyme activity | unchanged `AR` | Implied gene-centric erythropoietic porphyria classification | Straightforward rename and definition refinement | **Actionable** |\n| `15-16` | `UROD` | Parent/current term `MONDO:0100498 Porphyria cutanea tarda`; child/additional listed `MONDO:0015104 Porphyria, hepatoerythropoietic` | `TERM Update (update definition + relabel)` plus lumping | `UROD-related porphyria` | Semidominant spectrum due to monoallelic and biallelic `UROD` variants; environmental factors usually contributory; monoallelic adult episodic photosensitivity, biallelic childhood photosensitivity/liver damage | revised to `Semidominant` from `AD (mostly), AR` | Explicit lump: previous disease entities should be child terms. Additional request names child diseases: `hepatoerythropoietic porphyria` and `porphyria cutanea tarda` | Gene-centric classification but no explicit primary site label in rationale, unlike others | **Actionable** |\n| `17-18` | `CPOX` | Parent/current term `MONDO_0800180 Coproporphyria`; child/additional listed `MONDO:0007369 Harderoporphyria` | `TERM Update (update definition + relabel)` plus lumping | `CPOX-related hepatic porphyria` | Semidominant spectrum due to monoallelic and biallelic `CPOX` variants; monoallelic acute neurovisceral attacks; biallelic infantile severe phenotype with jaundice, hepatosplenomegaly, erythrodontia, photosensitivity, etc. | revised to `Semidominant` from `AD (mostly), AR` | Explicit lump: previous disease entities should be child terms. Additional request names children: `Hereditary coproporphyria (AD)` and `Harderoporphyria (AR)` | Current sheet only gives a MONDO ID for `Harderoporphyria`, not for a separate `Hereditary coproporphyria` term, so existing MONDO structure may need inspection | **Actionable, with follow-up check** |\n| `19-20` | `PPOX` | No parent MONDO ID for proposed parent. Existing terms listed: `MONDO:0008297 Variegate porphyria`; child/additional `MONDO:0957577 Variegate porphyria, childhood-onset` | `NEW MONDO PARENT TERM: PPOX-related hepatic porphyria` plus lumping | New parent: `PPOX-related hepatic porphyria` | Semidominant spectrum due to monoallelic and biallelic `PPOX` variants; monoallelic adolescent/adult episodic disease; biallelic childhood/adolescent severe disease with developmental and dysmorphic features | revised to `Semidominant` from current `AD` plus child row `AR` | Explicit lump: prior disease entities should be child terms. Additional request names: `Autosomal dominant variegate porphyria` and `Autosomal recessive variegate porphyria` | Requires creation of a new parent term and likely review of whether existing `Variegate porphyria` and `Variegate porphyria, childhood-onset` map cleanly to AD/AR child concepts | **Actionable, but multi-step** |\n| `21` | `FECH` | `MONDO:0008319`; disease label `protoporphyria, erythropoietic, 1` | `TERM Update (update definition + relabel)` | `FECH-related erythropoietic protoporphyria` | AR erythropoietic protoporphyria due to `biallelic FECH` variants; typically PPIX accumulation; often one hypomorphic allele in trans to pathogenic allele; clinically indistinguishable from ALAS2-related EPP | unchanged `AR` | Implied gene-centric erythropoietic porphyria classification | Straightforward rename/definition update request | **Actionable** |\n\n**Rows that look directly actionable**\n- `ALAS2`\n- `ALAD`\n- `UROS`\n- `UROD`\n- `CPOX`\n- `FECH`\n\nThese are mostly straightforward `rename + definition update`, with some also requesting explicit lumping under a gene-centric parent term.\n\n**Rows that are actionable but structurally more complex**\n- `HMBS`\n- `PPOX`\n\nThese require:\n- creating a new gene-centric parent term,\n- reparenting existing disease terms under it,\n- reconciling AD/AR presentations into a `semidominant` spectrum model,\n- and for `HMBS`, creating a new child term for `acute intermittent porphyria nonerythroid variant`.\n\n**Main ambiguities / unresolved questions to check before curation**\n1. `MONDO_...` formatting:\n   - Several IDs use underscore notation, e.g. `MONDO_0013000`, `MONDO_0958224`.\n   - These likely mean `MONDO:...`, but should be verified in ontology before action.\n\n2. Missing MONDO IDs for proposed new parent terms:\n   - `HMBS-related hepatic porphyria`\n   - `PPOX-related hepatic porphyria`\n   - likely new terms need to be created.\n\n3. Missing MONDO ID for `acute intermittent porphyria nonerythroid variant`:\n   - Sheet says `NOT AVAILABLE`, so this appears to be a new term request.\n\n4. Scope of lumping vs relabeling:\n   - For `UROD`, `CPOX`, `PPOX`, and `HMBS`, the sheet wants gene-centric parent terms with prior disease entities as children.\n   - This implies ontology restructuring, not just simple renaming.\n\n5. Whether some listed current labels are OMIM-style names rather than exact current MONDO labels:\n   - Example: `protoporphyria, erythropoietic, 1`\n   - Example: `Porphyria, acute hepatic`\n   - These should be checked against current MONDO names before editing.\n\n6. Child-term granularity for `PPOX` and `CPOX`:\n   - Sheet refers to `Autosomal dominant ...` and `Autosomal recessive ...` disease names, but only some existing MONDO child IDs are provided.\n   - Need to verify whether existing MONDO child terms already cover those concepts or if new ones are needed.\n\n**Practical curation takeaway**\n- Treat the workbook as proposing a broad shift to `gene-centric porphyria grouping`, often organized by `primary site of heme synthesis affected`:\n  - `erythropoietic` for `ALAS2`, `UROS`, `FECH`\n  - `hepatic` for `ALAD`, `HMBS`, `CPOX`, `PPOX`\n  - `UROD-related porphyria` is gene-centric but not explicitly restricted to hepatic/erythropoietic in the requested revised label\n- The simplest rows are mostly relabel/definition updates.\n- The hardest rows are the ones introducing new parent terms and spectrum-based semidominant classification.\n\nIf useful, I can turn this into a curator-ready checklist with one action item list per MONDO term.\n</task_result>","metadata":{"parentSessionId":"ses_1cc82e6b8ffeZCRAO8D6mymYrV","sessionId":"ses_1cc81ea29ffe1gjhh0yCubHcML","model":{"modelID":"gpt-5.4","providerID":"codexoauth"},"truncated":false},"title":"parse porphyria spreadsheet","time":{"start":1778980361712,"end":1778980431186}},"id":"prt_e337e09a70015lOLGtz30Pb4oy","sessionID":"ses_1cc82e6b8ffeZCRAO8D6mymYrV","messageID":"msg_e337e03a3001t6Rh6jAWzeMuaV"}}
