itary coproporphyria, with a semidominant mode of inheritance.\n\n  Line 621417: def: \"A rare semidominant genetic skeletal disorder caused by a variation in ACAN gene, characterized by short stature with variable phenotypic features which may include osteochondritis dissecans, advanced bone age, early-onset arthritis, and/or features consistent with spondyloepiphyseal dysplasia, Kimberley type caused by a single allele whereas biallelic variation can cause spondyloepimetaphyseal dysplasia, aggrecan type.\" [PMID:27311816, PMID:35434101]\n","metadata":{"matches":6,"truncated":false},"title":"semidominant|semi-dominant","time":{"start":1778980524641,"end":1778980524689}},"id":"prt_e33809252001MALClY25bkpC8f","sessionID":"ses_1cc82e6b8ffeZCRAO8D6mymYrV","messageID":"msg_e33803f3c001jSIG8ZoZJcqTlV"}}
