{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1778980893889,"sessionID":"ses_1cc82e6b8ffeZCRAO8D6mymYrV","part":{"id":"prt_e338634be001caZSjbEj882z0H","messageID":"msg_e33863451001pU8OJzhYSSPDxS","sessionID":"ses_1cc82e6b8ffeZCRAO8D6mymYrV","snapshot":"0d17186d7ae2e43817fc3ae6b93d41096791e557","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778980906586,"sessionID":"ses_1cc82e6b8ffeZCRAO8D6mymYrV","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"skill","callID":"call_fOkiN80RrUJBGHDNPuyEP6Vf","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"name":"odk"},"output":"<skill_content name=\"odk\">\n# Skill: odk\n\n# Running ODK commands in this repo\n\n## TL;DR\n\n`src/ontology/run.sh` is the official wrapper, but it ends in `docker run -ti` so it **fails silently in any non-TTY context** (Claude Code, CI, non-interactive shells) with `the input device is not a TTY` and exits without running the command.\n\nIf you have a TTY, prefer `run.sh`. If you don't, call docker directly with `-i` only.\n\n## When you have a TTY (interactive terminal)\n\n```bash\ncd src/ontology && sh run.sh <command> <args...>\n```\n\nExamples:\n```bash\nsh run.sh make NORM\nsh run.sh owltools --use-catalog mondo-edit.obo --obsolete-replace MONDO:A MONDO:B -o -f obo mondo-edit.obo\nsh run.sh robot verify --catalog catalog-v001.xml -i mondo-edit.obo --queries ../sparql/qc/general/qc-foo.sparql -O reports/\n```\n\n## When you don't have a TTY (Claude Code, CI, scripts)\n\nSymptom: `sh run.sh <anything>` prints `the input device is not a TTY` and exits with no further output, no file changes.\n\nWorkaround — invoke docker directly using the same image and mounts as `run.sh`, but with `-i` only:\n\n```bash\ndocker run --memory=8g \\\n  -v /ABSOLUTE/PATH/TO/REPO:/work \\\n  -w /work/src/ontology \\\n  -e ROBOT_JAVA_ARGS=-Xmx8G -e JAVA_OPTS=-Xmx8G \\\n  --rm -i obolibrary/odkfull:<TAG-FROM-RUN.SH> \\\n  <command> <args...>\n```\n\nWhere:\n- `/ABSOLUTE/PATH/TO/REPO` = the repo root (the parent of `src/`).\n- `<TAG-FROM-RUN.SH>` = whatever tag is set in `IMAGE=` in `src/ontology/run.sh`. **Always read `run.sh` first to look up the current tag** — do not hardcode `v1.6` or any other version.\n\n## Reading the right image tag\n\nDon't memorize the version. The line in `run.sh` is the source of truth:\n\n```bash\ngrep '^IMAGE=' src/ontology/run.sh\n# IMAGE=${IMAGE:-odkfull:v1.6}\n```\n\n## Common ODK commands you'll need\n\n| What | Command body (after `run.sh` or after the `docker run ... -i obolibrary/odkfull:<TAG>` prefix) |\n|---|---|\n| Normalize edit file | `make NORM` then `mv NORM mondo-edit.obo` (run from `src/ontology`) |\n| Convert / syntax check | `robot convert --catalog catalog-v001.xml -i mondo-edit.obo -f obo -o mondo-edit.TMP.obo` |\n| Run a QC query | `robot verify --catalog catalog-v001.xml -i mondo-edit.obo --queries ../sparql/qc/general/qc-X.sparql -O reports/` |\n| Merge / obsolete with replacement | `owltools --use-catalog mondo-edit.obo --obsolete-replace MONDO:A MONDO:B -o -f obo mondo-edit.obo` |\n\n## Notes\n\n- All ODK commands assume CWD is `src/ontology/`.\n- `make NORM` writes to a file called `NORM` in `src/ontology/`. You must `mv NORM mondo-edit.obo` afterward.\n- `robot verify` exits non-zero on QC failures and writes one TSV per failing query under `-O reports/`. Empty exit + `PASS Rule ... 0 violation(s)` = clean.\n- If `run.sh` reports `the input device is not a TTY`, do **not** retry the same command — it will keep failing. Switch to the docker-direct invocation.\n\nBase directory for this skill: file:///__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/.agents/skills/odk\nRelative paths in this skill (e.g., scripts/, reference/) are relative to this base directory.\nNote: file list is sampled.\n\n<skill_files>\n\n</skill_files>\n</skill_content>","metadata":{"name":"odk","dir":"/__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/.agents/skills/odk","truncated":false},"title":"Loaded skill: odk","time":{"start":1778980906573,"end":1778980906584}},"id":"prt_e33866643001hfoGaKedvACqF1","sessionID":"ses_1cc82e6b8ffeZCRAO8D6mymYrV","messageID":"msg_e33863451001pU8OJzhYSSPDxS"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778980906651,"sessionID":"ses_1cc82e6b8ffeZCRAO8D6mymYrV","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_o5p2J2oVDZ26aJ8a1BzeNsfW","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/terms/porphyria_9703_new_terms.obo","offset":1,"limit":200},"output":"<path>/__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/terms/porphyria_9703_new_terms.obo</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: [Term]\n2: id: MONDO:7770003\n3: name: HMBS-related hepatic porphyria\n4: def: \"A semidominant hepatic porphyria caused by monoallelic or biallelic variants in the HMBS gene. Monoallelic variants typically cause acute intermittent porphyria with neurovisceral attacks, whereas biallelic variants can cause a severe childhood-onset neurologic phenotype that may include developmental abnormalities, ataxia, dysarthria, leukoencephalopathy, cataracts, and optic nerve hypoplasia.\" [https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9703, https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40097/]\n5: subset: clingen {source=\"MONDO:CLINGEN\"}\n6: subset: rare\n7: is_a: MONDO:0002520 {source=\"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9703\", source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40097/\"} ! hepatic porphyria\n8: intersection_of: MONDO:0002520 ! hepatic porphyria\n9: intersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/4982 ! HMBS\n10: relationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/4982 {source=\"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9703\", source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40097/\"} ! HMBS\n11: property_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator doi:10.1186/s13326-024-00320-3\n12: property_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9703\" xsd:anyURI\n13: \n14: [Term]\n15: id: MONDO:7770004\n16: name: acute intermittent porphyria nonerythroid variant\n17: def: \"An HMBS-related hepatic 