{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778981013012,"sessionID":"ses_1cc82e6b8ffeZCRAO8D6mymYrV","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_RdmQms9z1tGifhQfm2CzNlyk","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n+Addressed in PR #<NN>.\n+\n+Summary:\n+- Updated ClinGen-requested porphyria gene-disease labels/definitions for `ALAS2`, `ALAD`, `UROS`, `FECH`, `UROD`, and `CPOX`.\n+- Added new spectrum parent terms for `HMBS`-related and `PPOX`-related hepatic porphyria, plus a new child term for acute intermittent porphyria nonerythroid variant.\n+- Reparented the relevant existing HMBS/PPOX/CPOX child terms under those gene-centric spectrum terms.\n+\n+One conservative decision was made for the `UROD` branch: because MONDO already distinguishes sporadic and familial porphyria cutanea tarda, I updated the `UROD` spectrum parent and linked hepatoerythropoietic porphyria to it without forcing all porphyria cutanea tarda under an inherited gene-spectrum term.\n*** Add File: /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/PR_COMMENTS.md\n+Implemented the porphyria updates requested in issue `#9703` using the attached ClinGen EIM spreadsheet as the source of truth.\n+\n+Changes made:\n+- Renamed and updated definitions for:\n+  - `MONDO:0010420` -> `ALAS2-related erythropoietic protoporphyria`\n+  - `MONDO:0013000` -> `ALAD-related hepatic porphyria`\n+  - `MONDO:0009902` -> `UROS-related erythropoietic porphyria`\n+  - `MONDO:0008319` -> `FECH-related erythropoietic protoporphyria`\n+  - `MONDO:0100498` -> `UROD-related porphyria`\n+  - `MONDO:0800180` -> `CPOX-related hepatic porphyria`\n+- Added new terms:\n+  - `MONDO:7770003` `HMBS-related hepatic porphyria`\n+  - `MONDO:7770004` `acute intermittent porphyria nonerythroid variant`\n+  - `MONDO:7770005` `PPOX-related hepatic porphyria`\n+- Reparented existing terms into the requested gene-centric spectrum structure:\n+  - `acute intermittent porphyria`, `encephalopathy, porphyria-related`, and `leukoencephalopathy, porphyria-related` under `HMBS-related hepatic porphyria`\n+  - `variegate porphyria` and `variegate porphyria, childhood-onset` under `PPOX-related hepatic porphyria`\n+  - `hereditary coproporphyria` and `harderoporphyria` under `CPOX-related hepatic porphyria`\n+  - `hepatoerythropoietic porphyria` under `UROD-related porphyria`\n+\n+Rationale:\n+- The spreadsheet requests a shift to gene-centric porphyria classification, especially for multi-allelic disease spectra where monoallelic and biallelic presentations are being treated as a single ClinGen disease entity.\n+- The HMBS and PPOX requests explicitly required new parent terms and a new HMBS subtype term, so those were added as new `MONDO:777xxxx` terms.\n+- The `CPOX` parent already existed in MONDO, but it still carried an older `hereditary coproporphyria` framing and a gain-of-function relation inconsistent with the current ClinGen comment; this was aligned to the requested hepatic spectrum model.\n+- For `UROD`, I kept the change conservative because MONDO already separates sporadic and familial porphyria cutanea tarda. I updated the `UROD` gene-spectrum parent and attached `hepatoerythropoietic porphyria`, but did not force all `porphyria cutanea tarda` under the inherited gene-spectrum term.\n+\n+Validation performed:\n+- Downloaded and reconstructed the attached spreadsheet to recover the actual requested term-by-term changes rather than inferring from the issue body alone.\n+- Checked the affected MONDO stanzas out through the standard `obo-checkout.pl` / `obo-checkin.pl` workflow.\n+- Ran `robot convert --catalog src/ontology/catalog-v001.xml -i src/ontology/mondo-edit.obo -f obo -o /tmp/opencode/mondo-edit.TMP.obo` successfully after integration.\n+\n+Constraints / follow-up notes:\n+- The repo guidance requests normalization via ODK (`make NORM`), but the evaluation environment did not provide `docker`, so that step could not be executed here.\n+- One checked-out helper file remained in `terms/` after check-in (`terms/MONDO_0015104.obo`) because that term was reviewed but not edited. It was not committed.\n+\n+Completed checklist:\n+- [x] Read issue context and recover the attached spreadsheet contents\n+- [x] Inspect current porphyria MONDO terms before editing\n+- [x] Apply requested relabeling/definition updates\n+- [x] Create required new parent and child terms\n+- [x] Reparent existing terms into the requested gene-centric structure\n+- [x] Run post-edit ontology conversion validation\n+- [x] Commit only `src/ontology/mondo-edit.obo`\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\nA PR_COMMENTS.md","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n===================================================================\n--- /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n+++ /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,8 @@\n+Addressed in PR #<NN>.\n+\n+Summary:\n+- Updated ClinGen-requested porphyria gene-disease labels/definitions for `ALAS2`, `ALAD`, `UROS`, `FECH`, `UROD`, and `CPOX`.\n+- Added new spectrum parent terms for `HMBS`-related and `PPOX`-related hepatic porphyria, plus a new child term for acute intermittent porphyria nonerythroid variant.\n+- Reparented the relevant existing HMBS/PPOX/CPOX child terms under those gene-centric spectrum terms.\n+\n+One conservative decision was made for the `UROD` branch: because MONDO already distinguishes sporadic and familial porphyria cutanea tarda, I updated the `UROD` spectrum parent and linked hepatoerythropoietic porphyria to it without forcing all porphyria cutanea tarda under an inherited gene-spectrum term.\n\nIndex: /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/PR_COMMENTS.md\n===================================================================\n--- /__w/eval-ont-ag